WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.030
- You know those mornings when you wake up

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.130
and you're still like drunk,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.740
that is 100% where I'm at right now.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.522
Let's drunk dance.

00:00:08.522 --> 00:00:11.939
(funky bass dance music)

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.230
Okay so I met this dude
who was living in Prague,

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.460
and he told me that every morning,

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.810
the first things he'd do
when he woke up was dance,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.850
with reckless abandon
like no one was watching.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.170
He said it helped with
his self confidence,

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.920
make him feel less awkward or silly,

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.010
because he did the silliest thing

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.240
he could think of in the morning.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.490
Challenged Brenda, Jade
and Eric and myself,

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.600
to do the same thing.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.120
We're going to dance with reckless abandon

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.070
for three songs every
morning for five days.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.440
And we put together a little playlist

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.250
for each of us on Spotify which you can

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.850
get in the descriptions below.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.039
This is going to be awkward
as hell, let's do this.

00:00:43.039 --> 00:00:44.020
(alarm beeping)

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.100
- All right, so I just woke up,

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.830
and I'm actually really excited,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:47.663
I'm ready to do this.

00:00:47.663 --> 00:00:49.142
Time to get up and dance.

00:00:49.142 --> 00:00:51.642
(dance music)

00:00:56.413 --> 00:00:57.246
♪ Ay oh DJ ♪

00:00:57.246 --> 00:00:59.496
♪ Ay oh DJ ♪

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.900
- Oh my God I'm tired!

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.120
That was a great way to wake up.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.513
I feel frickin amazing.

00:01:06.513 --> 00:01:08.654
- I feel like today, (snaps fingers)

00:01:08.654 --> 00:01:10.441
Mine, like that.

00:01:10.441 --> 00:01:14.202
I feel like today the cats
in this frickin onesie

00:01:14.202 --> 00:01:17.463
are giving me all of their power.

00:01:17.463 --> 00:01:20.640
- I went for Erkwerks Birthday last night.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.375
And I am massively hung over.

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:25.042
But today, I choose,

00:01:26.935 --> 00:01:28.244
dance.

00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:31.077
(rock beat music)

00:01:39.393 --> 00:01:42.153
Morning dances (stumbling)

00:01:42.153 --> 00:01:44.820
may help hangovers, but
they don't cure hangovers.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.700
- Good morning.

00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.666
(groovy dance music)

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.560
- [Clark] How was it?

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:02.393
- Ugh

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.590
- It helps you defeat,

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:11.390
the one obstacle, your mind man

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.650
your mind, you crazy, you crazy.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.910
- It's very freeing, it's
very freeing to dance,

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.850
and not care what anyone thinks of you.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:22.040
- As you can tell by my
dance moves, I'm not,

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.900
I'm not dancing for style.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.230
I'm dancing for me.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.110
I think this is

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.000
the toughest workout I've
had of this so far man.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.810
- This is gonna be a fun
little, good bye dance

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.139
to you guys, but I'm gonna keep dancin so.

00:02:35.139 --> 00:02:38.472
(festive upbeat music)

00:02:50.059 --> 00:02:52.059
♪ Whee ♪

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.310
- Man, this is definitely
a fun way to work out,

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.300
definitely a fun way to
keep your resolution going.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.640
I might keep this up.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.660
- I really really truly
recommend this challenge,

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.190
I think you should try and
do something in the morning

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.530
that's positive and wakes you up.

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:17.930
Anything that puts you in a good mood,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.450
make sure to do it in the morning,

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.320
because that's what starts
off the rest of your day.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.330
- In the comfort of your bedroom,

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.090
you can dance like a fool,

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.290
dance like nobody's watching.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.710
Just like, get in tune, makes you happy,

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.750
dancing is exercise, dudes.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.210
Look how out of breath I am.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:33.464
- Of course I've learned that,

00:03:33.464 --> 00:03:34.297
I think I'm gonna keep doing this,

00:03:34.297 --> 00:03:37.680
maybe not so much, like everyday,

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.130
but, well who knows, maybe,

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.064
I don't know, maybe who knows?

00:03:42.064 --> 00:03:45.481
(upbeat energetic music)

